Opportunities are developing in renewable hydrogen certification, e-fuel and ammonia project assessments, annual surveillance and international chain-of-custody verification. Export-oriented producers may also seek pre-certification reviews to assess whether proposed project structures align with target-market requirements.

Regional Market Insights
Europe accounted for an estimated 64% of the market in 2025, supported by established certification frameworks, regulatory requirements and the presence of recognised verification organisations.

Asia-Pacific offers opportunities through renewable hydrogen and ammonia project development, particularly among export-oriented producers. North America is developing its renewable fuel certification ecosystem, while Latin America and the Middle East and Africa may benefit from projects targeting international fuel markets.

